# Class diagrams (domain model)

Three diagrams, split like the ER diagrams in SAD 6.3. Attribute names are the column names of the table catalogue (SAD 6.4). Only the key attributes are drawn. Types are shown where the attribute is an enumeration, and the values are in the tables under each diagram. Fields that end in `_enc` are encrypted at field level.

Where the ER diagram and the table catalogue differ, these diagrams follow the table catalogue: a user and a blood center are optional on the other side (`center_id` and `institution_id` are nullable), and a storage temperature log belongs to a center (`center_id`), not to a unit.

